/-!
# Linear forms at the six SHA-2 parameter sets

GENERATED by `MReduction/gen/gen.py` from the SHA2-128s instances of `security/Reduction`
(`Linear.lean`, `LinearBytes.lean`) by the substitution `Link.vp ↦ S.vp`, `Link.prims ↦ S.prims`, `codec128s ↦ codec S`,
`structural_128s ↦ structural S` (the forger variable `S` of the originals is called `F`).
Every theorem is the generic theorem of `Reduction` of the same base name at `structural S`.

Naming: `MReduction.slhdsa_sha2_<base> (S : Sha2Set)` generic,
`MReduction.slhdsa_sha2_<set>_<base>` per set (`<set>` = 128s, 128f, 192s, 192f, 256s, 256f), where
`<base>` is the name of `Reduction.slhdsa_sha2_128s_<base>` (for the originals named
`slhdsa_<x>_128s`, `<base> = <x>`).
-/

